      "page_title": "Async Comprehensions & Class-Based Managers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Async object → `async with` / `async for`. Async generators (page 7) write `__aiter__`/`__anext__` for you."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Comprehensions and contextlib",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def main():",
            "    a = [x async for x in src]",
            "    b = [await f(x) for x in xs]",
            "    # b awaits one by one (serial)"
          ],
          "note": "valid only inside async def"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async for` in a comp → awaits `__anext__` per item",
            "`await` in a comp → runs f(x) **serially**",
            "Set and dict comps work too: `{k async for k in src}`",
            "Filters allowed: `[x async for x in src if x]`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# concurrent instead of serial",
            "b = await asyncio.gather(",
            "    *(f(x) for x in xs))",
            "# same order as xs"
          ],
          "note": "gather runs all f(x) at once"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`with Pool():` → **TypeError**: does not support the context manager protocol",
            "`for r in Pages(api):` → **TypeError**: object is not iterable",
            "`async def __aiter__` → `async for` receives a coroutine and fails",
            "Async comprehension outside `async def` → SyntaxError",
            "`return True` in `__aexit__` by accident **hides** every error"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Example: class-based manager",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class Timer:",
            "  async def __aenter__(self):",
            "    self.t0 = time.perf_counter()",
            "    return self",
            "  async def __aexit__(self, *exc):",
            "    self.dt = time.perf_counter()-self.t0"
          ],
          "note": "returns None → errors propagate"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "`__aexit__` returns",
            "Exception"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`None` / `False`",
              "**re-raised**"
            ],
            [
              "`True`",
              "==suppressed=="
            ],
            [
              "raises new error",
              "replaces original"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "When to write a class",
          "text": "Need state or reuse → class with `__aenter__`/`__aexit__`. One-off setup/teardown → ==@asynccontextmanager==."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
