      "page_title": "Common Bugs and How to Catch Them",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Awaits and Lost Tasks",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`fetch()` without **await** returns a coroutine object that never runs",
            "Python warns: `RuntimeWarning: coroutine ... was never awaited`",
            "The loop keeps only ==weak refs==, so an unreferenced task can be GC'd mid-run",
            "'Task exception was never retrieved' means a background task **failed** silently"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "bg = set()",
            "t = asyncio.create_task(job())",
            "bg.add(t)          # strong ref",
            "t.add_done_callback(bg.discard)",
            "await t   # surfaces its error"
          ],
          "note": "or just use a TaskGroup"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Blocking the Loop",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Blocks every task",
            "Async fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`time.sleep(1)`",
              "`await asyncio.sleep(1)`"
            ],
            [
              "`requests.get()`",
              "{icon:python} aiohttp / httpx"
            ],
            [
              "heavy CPU loop",
              "`await to_thread(fn)`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "asyncio.run(main(), debug=True)",
            "# shell: PYTHONASYNCIODEBUG=1",
            "# logs slow callbacks (>100ms)",
            "# + never-awaited coroutines"
          ],
          "note": "turn on in dev and tests"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Cancellation and Loops",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bare `except:` or `except BaseException` that doesn't re-raise **swallows** ==CancelledError==",
            "That breaks `task.cancel()` and every timeout",
            "`asyncio.run()` inside a running loop (Jupyter) raises **RuntimeError**. Use `await main()` there",
            "A Lock or session shared across loops raises 'attached to a different loop'"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "    await work()",
            "except asyncio.CancelledError:",
            "    await cleanup()",
            "    raise      # ALWAYS re-raise"
          ],
          "note": "never swallow CancelledError"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Sessions and Races",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ClientSession that is never closed warns 'Unclosed client session'",
            "One session **per request** wastes connection pooling",
            "Check-then-act across an ==await== with no Lock causes duplicate work (see p.4)"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with ClientSession() as s:",
            "    await gather(*(get(s, u)",
            "        for u in urls))"
          ],
          "note": "one session per app"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# no lock: 2 tasks both fetch",
            "async with lock:",
            "    if k not in cache:",
            "        cache[k] = await fetch(k)"
          ],
          "note": "the await is the race window"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Error Message → Fix",
          "ink": "green"
        },
